                            <resolved>Wed, 6 May 2015 12:16:44 +0000</resolved>
                                    <version>sprint-4</version>
                                    <fixVersion>sprint-4</fixVersion>
                                        <due></due>
                            <votes>0</votes>
                                    <watches>1</watches>
                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="14529171" author="agura" created="Tue, 5 May 2015 20:01:55 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;  1. OOM isn&apos;t TTL manager problem. Indeed it is &lt;tt&gt;GridCacheMapEntry.onTtlExpired&lt;/tt&gt; bug that leads to &lt;tt&gt;GridDhtAtomicCacheEntry&lt;/tt&gt; instance leaks.&lt;br/&gt;
  2. It is related with example itself: two queries execute sequentially, but data set have changed when second query started.&lt;br/&gt;
  3. CPU usage is very high (even streaming stopped) because cleanup worker infinitely runs but user threads don&apos;t help to it. It is bug in &lt;tt&gt;DataStreamerImpl.IsolatedUpdater.receive()&lt;/tt&gt; that doesn&apos;t force eviction.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14530430" author="agura" created="Wed, 6 May 2015 12:18:21 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Merged into ignite-sprint-4 branch.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                    </comments>
